          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: xièjué",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "xièjué — \"to decline politely\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "wǒ qǐng tā chī fàn tā xièjué le — I invited him to dinner, but he politely declined."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Its characters come later; for now it is a word for the ear."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "xièjué is built from 谢 and jué, both inherited from Middle Chinese, zjaeH and dzjwet (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), which glosses the first 'to take leave' and the second 'to cut off'."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
